Q: Why is the terminal outputting &quot;0&quot; in this code? A: <p>Here you just initialize values, you don't set a law of how they change;</p>
<pre><code>long long n = 2;                   // 2 is assigned to variable n
long long lastn = n - 1;           // n-1 = 1, 1 is assigned to lastn
long long fibonnaci = n + lastn;   // 3 is assigned to fibonnaci 
</code></pre>
<p>C++ is an imperative language in its core, so you have to describe every step your program does.</p>
<p>Note, even values of fibonacci are a sequence of its own: 0, 2, 34, 144. The original sequence is a recursive sum, so our sequence a subset, containing every 3rd term.</p>
<p>It can be written as: <code>F{n} = 4*F{n-1} + F{n-2}</code>.</p>
<p>Summ of them can actually be found analitically, and summ of first N elements of Fibancci sequence or its subsequence is known, but that's not our goal here, is it?</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;

int main()
{
    constexpr unsigned fib_max = 4000000;  // maximum term value
    unsigned  fib_prev2 = 2;  // First even Fibonacci number
    unsigned  fib_prev1 = 8;       // Second even Fibonacci number
    unsigned  sum = fib_prev2;     // Initialize sum with the first even number

    // Calculate summ of each 3rd term until we reach
    // fibonaccy term greater than limit.
    // fib_prev1 here is fibonacci_3 from previous iteration
    while (fib_prev1 &lt; fib_max) { 
        sum += fib_prev1;

        unsigned  fibonacci_3 = 4 * fib_prev1 + fib_prev2;

        // Shift variables forward for the next iteration
        fib_prev2 = fib_prev1;
        fib_prev1 = fibonacci_3;
    }
    std::cout &lt;&lt; &quot;Sum = &quot; &lt;&lt; sum;
}
</code></pre>
<p>The loop above is an optimized version with O(log fib_max) cost, calculating only every 3rd  term of Fibonacci sequence..</p>
<p>I received answer <code>Sum = 4613732</code> which matches analytical solution.</p>
<p>By Binet's formula, the maximum index of term would be <code>floor (ln(4000000*sqrt(5))/ln((1+sqrt(5))/2)) = 33</code> and value of term will be <code>F{33} = 3524578</code>.</p>
<p>Summ of first N elements is <code>(F{N+2}-1)/2 = 4613732</code> for value of 33+2 = 35th term being <code>F{35} = 9227465</code>.</p>
